Overview of the code
--------------------

The following files implement public API, declared in libintl.h:
  gettext.c:          gettext
  dgettext.c:         dgettext
  dcgettext.c:        dcgettext
  ngettext.c:         ngettext
  dngettext.c:        dngettext
  dcngettext.c:       dcngettext
  textdomain.c:       textdomain
  bindtextdom.c:      bindtextdomain
                      bind_textdomain_codeset

The following files implement private API.
  gettextP.h:     dcigettext.c:       __dcigettext
                                      _nl_find_msg
                                      _nl_default_dirname
                                      _nl_domain_bindings
                                      _nl_default_default_domain
                                      _nl_current_default_domain
                  finddomain.c:       _nl_find_domain
                  loadmsgcat.c:       _nl_load_domain
                                      _nl_msg_cat_cntr
  loadinfo.h:     l10nflist.c:        _nl_make_l10nflist
                                      _nl_normalize_codeset
                  localealias.c:      _nl_expand_alias
                  explodename.c:      _nl_explode_name
  plural-exp.h:   plural.y:           __gettext_free_exp
                                      __gettextparse
                  plural-exp.c:       __gettext_germanic_plural
                                      __gettext_extract_plural
                  eval-plural.h:      plural_eval

Other files:

  gmo.h:          Describes the GNU MO file format.
  hash-string.h:  hash-string.c:      __hash_string

Overview of invocation hierarchy
--------------------------------

gettext
dgettext
 \-> dcgettext
       \-> __dcigettext

ngettext
dngettext
 \-> dcngettext
       \-> __dcigettext

The main general translation lookup function is __dcigettext.
__dcigettext
  \-> guess_category_value
  \-> _nl_find_domain
        \-> _nl_expand_alias
        \-> _nl_explode_name
              \-> _nl_normalize_codeset
        \-> _nl_make_l10nflist
        \-> _nl_load_domain
  \-> _nl_find_msg
        \-> _nl_load_domain
        \-> __hash_string
        \-> get_output_charset
  \-> plural_lookup
        \-> plural_eval

_nl_load_domain loads a MO file into memory.
_nl_load_domain
  \-> _nl_find_msg (for the header entry only)
  \-> __gettext_extract_plural
        \-> __gettextparse
